#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504710} :activity/id #uuid "a539756c-0db8-538b-b46b-47ef7d1eb9af" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048871 :topic/id #uuid "c80985c0-d51a-5f21-9b71-21587d8d82cc" :topic/math-academy-id 3024} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504710 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504616 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359a0b0c-50e8-5345-975b-7a3b5f1bf014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504123} {:answer/id #uuid "45c11c78-2d68-5904-8031-3d3a0242f7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504158} {:answer/id #uuid "ce74393d-eae8-577c-a62b-226565601386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504382} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0f3d27-f2c4-53e6-a0dd-86a7157d57b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504416} {:answer/id #uuid "ee53d443-4dcf-58ab-8684-f164d88801ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504445}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504382} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c67064-cabf-594b-8138-f2a53ecff042" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "328730e5-b32c-5f55-aef8-1fdf6d6f55ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-94622" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $Y$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le m) & ={\\int }_{0}^{m}{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-y}{|}_{0}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "01cc5e7e-84c9-528b-a9ef-d7f70750a185" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504726}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0765ab3d-3d10-5726-81d6-bd3fb3946642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{3}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{1}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504045} {:answer/id #uuid "13871642-8ae3-5019-b1de-22bbf1065713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{4}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504065} {:answer/id #uuid "684c5f78-814e-5747-b4d4-6c46b4604d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{4}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{1}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504214} {:answer/id #uuid "bbbdb289-ed8a-528b-8848-b0b72bf5ac8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{3}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{3}{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504356} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfff1b7-44ec-5407-a9f4-73c259e92041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt[6]{2}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504415}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504065} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f1f10e-3dae-5b47-be1d-ec0989a80ffb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3057bfc-a8d8-5a19-9075-be23799b04aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-125715" :question/problem "Find the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{q}_{1}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}^{6}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{q}_{3}^{6}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{3}^{6}} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\sqrt[6]{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[6]{4}-\\sqrt[6]{\\frac{4}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1e906454-9530-5253-a6c1-cda94270f061"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504720 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1562c7b8-2b30-5c44-851a-2e77ad1d9ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504069} {:answer/id #uuid "4abd80bd-1a68-546f-8588-851943834de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504167} {:answer/id #uuid "8768fd37-4607-5f84-9457-21d0bf221790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504268} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0eba09-da59-5a8c-ac0e-a47d1fba2292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504274} {:answer/id #uuid "c9880874-5f4d-577f-a29e-8c891f85c246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504373}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504274} :answer-field/id #uuid "b021d4b8-9d31-550f-8894-f27be8d6ecdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f1b2358-54f2-52cf-a9df-c46a72812503" :question/math-academy-id "q-94714" :question/problem "Find the $60$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $Y$ is the number ${y}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le {y}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $60$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.6.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le {y}_{0.6}) & ={\\int }_{1}^{{y}_{0.6}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{y}|}_{1}^{{y}_{0.6}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $60$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}} & =0.6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}_{0.6}} & =0.4 \\\\ {y}_{0.6} & =\\frac{1}{0.4} \\\\ {y}_{0.6} & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "44882186-3aa7-55b0-9985-fbfa449cb9fc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504721}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504721 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aed5558-3986-50d7-b1f2-81753d74b873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504081} {:answer/id #uuid "3978a119-ff81-5c74-849d-d9dd5d8e9158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504133} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6cb7e1-9231-5421-81e5-f17c6d73d937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504277} {:answer/id #uuid "92f9b85f-813a-5ae6-862a-7c2bae09fbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504291} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4f0b16-dcc0-5510-825c-f040ca9cf4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504305}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504081} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9539fc-eb18-57bd-a7aa-1b80040b3b7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "158dc85d-a65b-564b-ba7e-be30418efec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125530" :question/problem "Find the $72.9$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $72.9$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.729.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.729}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{x}_{0.729}}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8}|}_{0}^{{x}_{0.729}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $72.9$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{8} & =0.729 \\\\ {x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =\\sqrt[3]{(8)(0.729)} \\\\ {x}_{0.729}^{\\frac{1}{2}} & =(2)(0.9) \\\\ {x}_{0.729} & =(1.8)^{2} \\\\ {x}_{0.729} & =3.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "44dd1ada-9d95-5d13-8839-831e39188195" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504715}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504726 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ae6daed-2b77-524b-9d07-34d38e4edd65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.323" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504191} {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa3869-3391-50cc-8156-b0014d62d258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504272} {:answer/id #uuid "adb2c746-a72d-5f18-bbd1-89f21fb79cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.735" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504330} {:answer/id #uuid "c91fb8c1-0fe8-5ab4-8c4f-8dddfac7a8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.464" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504370} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a2d7a4-971e-5d00-bab4-e733a4d23d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.189" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504435}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504370} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc675dd-7a38-5eec-ad05-1b9e422a82c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e2b4a0b2-77c3-5ed8-8555-0cfe3f01b758" :question/math-academy-id "q-94668" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{1}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {q}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{q}_{3}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {q}_{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\nIQR={q}_{3}-{q}_{1}=2\\sqrt{3}-2≈1.464\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "62be2f38-fa1c-5afd-b03f-11afbcfda04d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504720}}] :activity/title "Median, Quartiles and Percentiles of Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504027}]}
